{
  "answer": "You can define a dependency that depends on another dependency by using the `Depends` parameter in your `@app.dependency` decorator. For example:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import Depends\n\nasync def get_db():\n    # database logic\n    pass\n\nasync def get_other_data(db: object = Depends(get_db)):\n    # use db\n    pass\n```\n\nIn this example, `get_other_data` depends on `get_db` to be executed.",
